92186045417] [17592186511384 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8e701f23-45b5-584b-9ff7-052c5c629f38" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511456 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511456 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146226" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511456 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511456 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ | $\\frac{7}{27}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=0]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|0}=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511456 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "047bb67d-8c03-57ec-a81f-c32911be6893" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511456 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ | $\\frac{16}{27}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ | $\\frac{7}{27}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{11}{27}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{9}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{11}$ | $\\frac{7}{11}$ | $\\frac{3}{11}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=0] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)]-{\\mu }_{Y|0}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{9}{16}+{4}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}+{8}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{16}]-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =0+6+4-4 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511491 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511491 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146278" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511491 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511491 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|2}=5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511491 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4b9363aa-00d2-51a2-9bff-045f9cb8f2d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511491 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{5}{16}$ | $\\frac{5}{16}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)]-{\\mu }_{X|2}^{2} \\\\  & =[{3}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+{9}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}]-{5}^{2} \\\\  & =6+27-25 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511574 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511574 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146236" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511574 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511574 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=5$ | $Y=10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{25}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{25}$ | $\\frac{1}{25}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=6]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|6}=\\frac{15}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511574 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e9ff9199-1184-598e-a945-b789f3d5b0b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511574 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=5$ | $Y=10$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{25}$ | $\\frac{23}{25}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{25}$ | $\\frac{1}{25}$ | $\\frac{2}{25}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=5$ | $Y=10$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{20}{23}$ | $\\frac{3}{23}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=6] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,6)]-{\\mu }_{Y|6}^{2} \\\\  & =[{5}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{10}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}]-{(\\frac{15}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{2}+50-\\frac{225}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511582 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511318 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511582 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146282" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511582 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511582 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|2}=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511582 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa585366-16bd-5221-b5b1-a80000ac4783" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511582 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)]-{\\mu }_{X|2}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}]-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{2}+1-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511586 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511586 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0300a9fc-85df-55bb-885b-ea046fb4bb5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511586 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186511456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511606 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511606 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "30c58b82-3c11-5385-abbd-de1c4e8158be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511606 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186511574 #